From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 15:13:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] feature: switch the built-in panel off while the lid is
 shut

Closing the lid turns off the backlight. It does not disable the RandR
output, shrink the desktop or renumber the Xinerama heads, so a docked
machine with the lid shut keeps a region of its desktop that is physically
invisible and anything placed there is lost. Kicker is the visible symptom,
being pinned to one head, but any window can land in that region.

Switch the panel's output off while the lid is shut and put it back when it
opens. Read the mode, position and primary flag through RandR, which
reports them exactly, and leave the write to xrandr, which recomputes the
framebuffer size; doing that here too would mean reimplementing arithmetic
whose failure corrupts the screen rather than merely erring.

The safety rests on one path and it is deliberately unconditional. Lid open
restores the panel without consulting the setting, because a setting can be
turned off in between and the cost of skipping it is a machine whose lid is
open and whose screen is dark. Everything else is a refusal: never switch
off unless another output is already being driven, which is counted rather
than inferred from whether an external is connected, since connectedness
leaves a race in which the external vanishes between the check and the act;
verify afterwards and put the panel straight back if nothing survived; and
decline when the panel's current mode cannot be read, since a panel that
cannot be restored should not be switched off.

Identify the panel by the kernel's connector type, and refuse when more
than one is found: a dual-panel laptop has two and only one is behind the
lid. Drivers that do not use those names match nothing, which is the
correct outcome rather than a wrong guess.

Do it before locking, so the locker draws once on the final geometry rather
than resizing underneath itself.

Restore at startup too, when the lid is open and a panel is found switched
off, for the case where the process that switched it off did not survive to
put it back. Nothing recorded that configuration then, so it comes back at
its preferred mode.

Default off. The setting beside it defaults on because its worst outcome is
a machine that stays awake; this one's is a display nobody can see.

Signed-off-by: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
